    {
      "topLeftX": 202,
      "topLeftY": 263,
      "bottomRightX": 353,
      "bottomRightY": 321,
      "content": "MB88303 has two modes for\nwriting data to the control\nregisters and display memory.\nThe modes are switched by the\nADM input.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 202,
      "topLeftY": 330,
      "bottomRightX": 306,
      "bottomRightY": 343,
      "content": "# Direct Address Mode",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 200,
      "topLeftY": 347,
      "bottomRightX": 349,
      "bottomRightY": 494,
      "content": "This mode is enabled when\ninput to the ADM terminal is\nlow. When the input signal to\nthe LDI terminal goes high,\ndata on DA7 to DA0 are\nlatched to the address\nregister. When the LDI\nterminal signal goes low,\n7 bits of data, DA6 to DA0,\nare written to the memory\nspecified by the memory\naddress register. Fig. 10(a) is\nthe timing diagram.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 202,
      "topLeftY": 503,
      "bottomRightX": 327,
      "bottomRightY": 515,
